# DAG: two grid/lengthscale experiments motivated by directly measuring the
# GP's fitting target's empirical correlation length in q (see memory
# manifold_correlation_length.md). TRAIN_Q012 builds the ls_min_q=0.12
# checkpoint (full 30-point grid); TRAIN_ADAPTIVE16 builds the adaptive-
# density 16-point grid checkpoint. Each SCAN is a DAG child of its own
# TRAIN and runs independently of the other pair.
#
# Submit from /scratch/wiay/daniel/heron-dense45 on wiay:
#   condor_submit_dag condor/dag_manifold_grid.dag
# Monitor: condor_q daniel -all ; tail -f condor/dag_manifold_grid.dag.dagman.out

JOB TRAIN_Q012      condor/train_pa_xas_lsminq012.sub
JOB SCAN_Q012       condor/scan_pa_xas_lsminq012.sub
JOB TRAIN_ADAPTIVE16 condor/train_pa_xas_adaptive16.sub
JOB SCAN_ADAPTIVE16  condor/scan_pa_xas_adaptive16.sub

PARENT TRAIN_Q012 CHILD SCAN_Q012
PARENT TRAIN_ADAPTIVE16 CHILD SCAN_ADAPTIVE16

RETRY TRAIN_Q012 1
RETRY SCAN_Q012 1
RETRY TRAIN_ADAPTIVE16 1
RETRY SCAN_ADAPTIVE16 1
